cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AuNa: Autonomous Navigation System Simulator"
message: >-
  If you use AuNa in your research, please cite both the software
  repository and the paper describing the framework.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Teper
    given-names: Harun
    email: harun.teper@tu-dortmund.de
    affiliation: "TU Dortmund University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HarunTeper/AuNa"
abstract: >-
  AuNa is an open-source ROS 2 framework and simulation testbed for
  reproducible autonomous-navigation and multi-robot experiments. It
  provides Gazebo-based multi-robot simulation, Nav2 integration,
  a Cooperative Adaptive Cruise Control (CACC) controller for platooning,
  wall following, EKF-based localization, ETSI ITS-G5 / V2X message
  handling with optional OMNeT++ network simulation, and a Docker Compose
  deployment for running complete cooperative-driving scenarios.
keywords:
  - ROS 2
  - robotics
  - autonomous driving
  - multi-robot systems
  - cooperative adaptive cruise control
  - platooning
  - Gazebo
  - simulation
  - V2X
license: MIT
